+
+The checked examples cover:
+
+* `_andBool_`: true/true and true/false;
+* `_+Int_`: `-7 + 11 = 4`;
+* `_*Int_`: `-4 * 5 = -20`;
+* `definedProjectInt`: true on injected Int and false on `noneV`;
+* `isInt`: true on the singleton injected-Int K sequence and false on an
+  injected Bool;
+* `project:Int`: recovers `-9`;
+* `projectIntTotal`: recovers `37`;
+* `project:Int?`: returns `some (-9)` on the projection domain and `none` on
+  injected Bool;
+* `applyBin`: Int multiplication, Int addition, and Int/Bool addition;
+* distinct inputs for addition, multiplication, and projection, rejecting
+  constant, identity, and zeroed behavior.
+
+COUNTERFACTUAL MUTATIONS
+
+The mutation file replaces load-bearing addition, total projection, and
+`applyBin` with constants.  Its assertions intentionally demand the honest
+results.
+
+COMMAND
+PATH=/opt/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.22.0/bin:$PATH \
+LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/proc_self_readlink.so \
+lake env lean BridgeMutationAudit.lean
+
+EXACT OUTPUT
+BridgeMutationAudit.lean:13:41: error: tactic 'rfl' failed, the left-hand side
+  constantPlus (-7) 11
+is not definitionally equal to the right-hand side
+  4
+⊢ constantPlus (-7) 11 = 4
+BridgeMutationAudit.lean:14:62: error: tactic 'rfl' failed, the left-hand side
+  constantProject (SortVal.inj_SortInt 37)
+is not definitionally equal to the right-hand side
+  37
+⊢ constantProject (SortVal.inj_SortInt 37) = 37
+BridgeMutationAudit.lean:18:36: error: tactic 'rfl' failed, the left-hand side
+  constantApplyBin "+" (SortVal.inj_SortInt (-7)) (SortVal.inj_SortInt 11)
+is not definitionally equal to the right-hand side
+  SortVal.inj_SortInt 4
+⊢ constantApplyBin "+" (SortVal.inj_SortInt (-7)) (SortVal.inj_SortInt 11) = SortVal.inj_SortInt 4
+
+EXIT STATUS
+1 (expected)
+
+BRIDGE JUDGMENT
+
+Every one of the nine target parameters has an exact candidate `def`.
+Its manifest `kore_symbol` and `source_rule_ids` agree with its use in the
+five frozen rules.  On the guarded operational domains, the definitions are
+the corresponding K hooks or projections:
+
+EXACT DEF LOCATIONS IN FRESH Proof.lean
+12:def _andBool_ (left right : SortBool) : SortBool :=
+16:def «_+Int_» (left right : SortInt) : SortInt :=
+20:def «_*Int_» (left right : SortInt) : SortInt :=
+108:def «applyBin(_,_,_)_MPY-CORE_Val_String_Val_Val»
+113:def «definedProjectInt(_)_VERIFICATION_Bool_Val» : SortVal → SortBool
+118:def isInt : SortK → SortBool
+123:def «project:Int» (term : SortK) : SortInt :=
+127:def projectIntTotal : SortVal → SortInt
+132:def «project:Int?» (term : SortK) : Option SortInt :=
+
+* Boolean conjunction is `Bool.and`; integer addition and multiplication are
+  Lean integer addition and multiplication.
+* `applyBin` dispatches `"*"` and `"+"` on injected Int values to those exact
+  operations; its extra cases do not alter the two bound rules.
+* `definedProjectInt` and `isInt` recognize precisely the Int injection in the
+  forms used by the frozen rules.
+* `project:Int`, `projectIntTotal`, and `project:Int?` recover precisely the
+  injected integer on their guarded domain.
+
+The frozen `projectIntTotal` is explicitly a total helper whose operational
+meaning is constrained only when `definedProjectInt` holds.  The candidate's
+zero fallback is therefore outside every relevant guarded use and does not
+make the proof convenient on the operational domain.  The bridge is not
+constant, hard-coded, identity-based, or vacuous.

